## 0) Key helper: “iterate only working days inside the span”

Add this inside `EmployeeSchedule` (same class as constraints), so constraints can call it.

```java
static Iterable<Integer> workingDayIdsIterable(Integer start, Integer days, String factory) {
    if (start == null || days == null || days <= 0) return List.of();
    final int s = start;
    final int e = start + days - 1;

    // Lazy iterator: no list allocation, skips closed days.
    return () -> new java.util.Iterator<>() {
        int cur = s;
        Integer next = null;

        private void pull() {
            while (next == null && cur <= e) {
                int d = cur++;
                if (isWorkingDay(d, factory)) {
                    next = d;
                    return;
                }
            }
        }

        @Override public boolean hasNext() {
            pull();
            return next != null;
        }
        @Override public Integer next() {
            pull();
            Integer out = next;
            next = null;
            return out;
        }
    };
}
```

Also add a **fast way to get seat timing** (use pinned span if pinned):

```java
static Integer seatStart(CrewSeat s, BlockDecision b) {
    return s.isPinned() ? s.pinnedStart : (b == null ? null : b.startDay);
}
static Integer seatDays(CrewSeat s, BlockDecision b) {
    return s.isPinned() ? s.pinnedDays : (b == null ? null : b.days);
}
