## 1) dailyCap12h (optimized)

No DaySlot join. We flatten days from each (seat, block).

```java
Constraint dailyCap12h(ConstraintFactory f) {
    var seatBlockDay = f.forEach(CrewSeat.class)
        .filter(s -> !isUnassigned(s.employee))
        .join(f.forEach(BlockDecision.class),
            Joiners.equal((CrewSeat s) -> s.blockId, (BlockDecision b) -> b.id))
        .filter((s, b) -> seatStart(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) > 0)
        // IMPORTANT: ignore pinnedFixed in "dynamic hours" sum; fixed part comes from FIXED_HOURS_BY_EMP_DAY
        .filter((s, b) -> !s.pinnedFixed)
        .flattenLast((s, b) -> workingDayIdsIterable(seatStart(s,b), seatDays(s,b), s.factory));

    return seatBlockDay
        .groupBy(
            (s, b, dayId) -> Arrays.asList(s.employee.id, dayId),
            ConstraintCollectors.sum((s, b, dayId) -> b.chosenHours())
        )
        .filter((key, dynHours) -> {
            int empId = (int) key.get(0);
            int dayId = (int) key.get(1);
            int fixedHours = FIXED_HOURS_BY_EMP_DAY
                .getOrDefault(empId, Collections.emptyMap())
                .getOrDefault(dayId, 0);
            return dynHours + fixedHours > DAILY_CAP;
        })
        .penalize(HardMediumSoftScore.ONE_HARD, (key, dynHours) -> {
            int empId = (int) key.get(0);
            int dayId = (int) key.get(1);
            int fixedHours = FIXED_HOURS_BY_EMP_DAY
                .getOrDefault(empId, Collections.emptyMap())
                .getOrDefault(dayId, 0);
            return (dynHours + fixedHours) - DAILY_CAP;
        })
        .asConstraint("seat-daily-cap-12h");
}
```

**Why faster:** complexity becomes proportional to “(assigned seats) × (days they work)”, not “all dayslots × all seats”.

