## 2) oneFactoryPerEmpPerDay (optimized)

Same flatten trick, group by (emp, day), collect dynamic factories, then union with fixed factories.

```java
Constraint oneFactoryPerEmpPerDay(ConstraintFactory f) {
    var seatBlockDay = f.forEach(CrewSeat.class)
        .filter(s -> !isUnassigned(s.employee))
        .join(f.forEach(BlockDecision.class),
            Joiners.equal((CrewSeat s) -> s.blockId, (BlockDecision b) -> b.id))
        .filter((s, b) -> seatStart(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) > 0)
        // ignore pinnedFixed in dynamic set; fixed fabs come from FIXED_FACTORIES_BY_EMP_DAY
        .filter((s, b) -> !s.pinnedFixed)
        .flattenLast((s, b) -> workingDayIdsIterable(seatStart(s,b), seatDays(s,b), s.factory));

    return seatBlockDay
        .groupBy(
            (s, b, dayId) -> Arrays.asList(s.employee.id, dayId),
            ConstraintCollectors.toSet((s, b, dayId) -> s.factory)
        )
        .filter((key, dynFabs) -> {
            int empId = (int) key.get(0);
            int dayId = (int) key.get(1);

            Set<String> fixedFabs = FIXED_FACTORIES_BY_EMP_DAY
                .getOrDefault(empId, Collections.emptyMap())
                .getOrDefault(dayId, Collections.emptySet());

            if (fixedFabs.isEmpty()) return dynFabs.size() > 1;

            Set<String> all = new HashSet<>(dynFabs);
            all.addAll(fixedFabs);
            return all.size() > 1;
        })
        .penalize(HardMediumSoftScore.ONE_HARD, (key, dynFabs) -> {
            int empId = (int) key.get(0);
            int dayId = (int) key.get(1);

            Set<String> fixedFabs = FIXED_FACTORIES_BY_EMP_DAY
                .getOrDefault(empId, Collections.emptyMap())
                .getOrDefault(dayId, Collections.emptySet());

            Set<String> all = new HashSet<>(dynFabs);
            all.addAll(fixedFabs);
            return all.size() - 1;
        })
        .asConstraint("seat-one-factory-per-emp-day");
}
```

