### 4.1) regionTransitGap (optimized)

Your old version does Uni↔Uni join across all emp-days, which can still be heavy.
But first, at least generate emp-days without DaySlot join:

```java
Constraint regionTransitGap(ConstraintFactory f) {
    var empDayUni = f.forEach(CrewSeat.class)
        .filter(s -> !isUnassigned(s.employee))
        .join(f.forEach(BlockDecision.class),
            Joiners.equal((CrewSeat s) -> s.blockId, (BlockDecision b) -> b.id))
        .filter((s, b) -> seatStart(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) > 0)
        .filter((s, b) -> !s.pinnedFixed)
        .flattenLast((s, b) -> workingDayIdsIterable(seatStart(s,b), seatDays(s,b), s.factory))
        .map((s, b, dayId) -> new EmpDay(s.employee.id, dayId, s.factory));

    return empDayUni
        .join(empDayUni,
            Joiners.equal(EmpDay::empId, EmpDay::empId),
            Joiners.lessThan(EmpDay::dayId, EmpDay::dayId))
        .filter((a, b) -> {
            String r1 = CAL.regionOfFab(a.factory());
            String r2 = CAL.regionOfFab(b.factory());
            int need = CAL.transitDays(r1, r2);
            if (need <= 0) return false;
            int delta = b.dayId() - a.dayId();
            return delta <= need;
        })
        .penalize(HardMediumSoftScore.ONE_HARD, (a, b) -> {
            String r1 = CAL.regionOfFab(a.factory());
            String r2 = CAL.regionOfFab(b.factory());
            int need  = CAL.transitDays(r1, r2);
            int delta = b.dayId() - a.dayId();
            return Math.max(1, need - delta + 1);
        })
        .asConstraint("emp-region-transit-gap");
}
```

**Even faster (recommended)**: add a filter to only compare nearby days (within max transit days), otherwise it’s still O(N²) per employee. If your max transit is, say, <= 7, do this:

```java
// replace Joiners.lessThan with:
Joiners.lessThan(EmpDay::dayId, EmpDay::dayId),
Joiners.filtering((a,b) -> (b.dayId() - a.dayId()) <= 10) // set to maxTransitDays+some buffer
```

You can compute `MAX_TRANSIT_DAYS` once from CAL.transitDays maps.

