### 4.2) regionStayMaxOn (optimized)

This one becomes much cheaper once day lists are built from flatten stream.

```java
Constraint regionStayMaxOn(ConstraintFactory f) {
    var empRegionDays = f.forEach(CrewSeat.class)
        .filter(s -> !isUnassigned(s.employee))
        .join(f.forEach(BlockDecision.class),
            Joiners.equal((CrewSeat s) -> s.blockId, (BlockDecision b) -> b.id))
        .filter((s, b) -> seatStart(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) != null && seatDays(s,b) > 0)
        .filter((s, b) -> !s.pinnedFixed)
        .flattenLast((s, b) -> workingDayIdsIterable(seatStart(s,b), seatDays(s,b), s.factory))
        .groupBy(
            (s, b, dayId) -> Arrays.asList(s.employee.id, CAL.regionOfFab(s.factory)),
            ConstraintCollectors.toList((s, b, dayId) -> dayId)
        )
        .filter((key, dayList) -> key.get(1) != null);

    return empRegionDays
        .filter((key, dayList) -> {
            String regionId = (String) key.get(1);
            int maxOn  = CAL.maxStayOn(regionId);
            int offInt = CAL.stayOffInterval(regionId);
            if (maxOn == Integer.MAX_VALUE) return false;
            int maxSpan = maxSegmentSpanWithBreak(dayList, offInt);
            return maxSpan > maxOn;
        })
        .penalize(HardMediumSoftScore.ONE_HARD, (key, dayList) -> {
            String regionId = (String) key.get(1);
            int maxOn  = CAL.maxStayOn(regionId);
            int offInt = CAL.stayOffInterval(regionId);
            int maxSpan = maxSegmentSpanWithBreak(dayList, offInt);
            return Math.max(1, maxSpan - maxOn);
        })
        .asConstraint("emp-region-stay-max-on");
}
```

