## 5) Extra speed wins (you should do these too)

### A) Reduce number of seats created

Right now you always create `w.maxHeads` seats, which can be huge. Create an upper bound that’s “enough to cover requiredHours”, not maxHeads.

Example inside `buildEntitiesSinglePass` when creating seats:

```java
int minAllowed = (w.allowed == null || w.allowed.isEmpty()) ? 8 : w.allowed.stream().mapToInt(x->x).min().orElse(8);
int maxAllowed = (w.allowed == null || w.allowed.isEmpty()) ? 8 : w.allowed.stream().mapToInt(x->x).max().orElse(8);

// estimate working days if fully spanning window (worst-case conservative)
int estD = workingDaysCount(w.startDayId, Math.max(1, w.endDayId - w.startDayId + 1), w.factory);
estD = Math.max(1, estD);

// seats needed if everyone works max hours:
int minSeatsToCover = (int) Math.ceil(req / (double)(maxAllowed * estD));
minSeatsToCover = Math.max(w.minHeads, minSeatsToCover);

// cap by maxHeads
int seatCount = Math.min(w.maxHeads, minSeatsToCover);

// create only seatCount
for (int sidx = 0; sidx < seatCount; sidx++) { ... }
```

This alone often gives a massive speedup.

